# Somebody else, in the next terminal. The line waits for the cache the
# session's own command writes — so the edit lands after the round boundary
# that reads the tree, in the same order a person in another window would
# manage — and then changes a tracked file this session never touched. There
# is no key that reaches outside the session, so the scene says it here.
( until [ -f .cache/gocache/aa/one ]; do sleep 0.2; done; sleep 2; printf 'and a line from the next terminal\n' >> notes.md ) & "$SHHH_BIN" code
